## 1. Objects and actual scope

Use the canonical contact-minimal then diameter-pair-minimal triangle-free global
source with D≥9. Retain all source points, including contact isolates. V is the
nonisolated positive-contact core, B is the full actual diameter endpoint set,
q=|B|, h=|H|, ν=ν(H), and x_B=b_out−q. The full supports C,H have positive
coefficients in a relative-interior normalized KKT stress. Canonical mixed rank
on V is 2|V|−3. All core point positions and edges are the original source objects.

Let I_r be the components of C[V\B], A_r their distinct loaded attachment sets,
a_r=|A_r|, n_r=|I_r|, e_r=|C[I_r]|, and t_r the number of contacts from I_r to B.
Use canonical notation

\[
 s_r=e_r+t_r-2n_r-1\ge0,\quad
 r_r=2n_r-\delta_r-2-e_r\ge0,\quad
 \delta_r=\operatorname{diam}_{graph}C[I_r],
\]

with δ_r=0 for a singleton. Define P_r=conv(A_r), d_r=diam(P_r).
Every |A_r|≥3. Canonical harmonic trapping puts I_r in P_r and
d_r≤δ_r+2. Section 62 gives the exact identity

\[
 \boxed{t_r=\delta_r+3+s_r+r_r.}                         \tag{1}
\]

Let J be all internal vertices of good unit-contact runs in same-carrier
diameter-leaf blocks. Every p∈J has its two neighboring leaves joined to p by
actual unit contacts. They and p share one actual diameter carrier. Let κ=q−|J|
count the remaining loaded vertices. Let N_r=|J∩A_r|.

## 2. Only O(ν+x_B) loaded vertices fail the good-fan test

The following rederives the relevant good-fan count from canonical Woodall
topology, rather than importing a report's unsupported equality.

### 2.1 Same-carrier leaves are contiguous

If p,q are diameter leaves with common carrier a, any loaded vertex z on the
open hull arc from p to q not containing a is also a leaf at a. For any other
diameter zw, the diameter-thrackle rule would make zw cross both ap and aq.
The permitted positions of w lie in disjoint hull arcs. Thus only za is possible.
This proves one consecutive leaf block per carrier.

Write P for the number of leaf-to-nonleaf diameter edges and c for the number
of carriers with such leaves. One pendant edge per carrier is a matching, so
c≤ν. The number of within-block loaded adjacencies is S=P−c.

In the forest branch, let K count isolated K_2 components and m count edges
between nonleaves. Woodall makes the nonleaf core a disjoint union of paths.
If its matching number is μ, m≤2μ and μ+K≤ν. Hence P=h−m−K≥h−2ν and
S≥h−3ν. In the odd-unicyclic branch with leaves, a pendant edge plus a
matching of the even path left after deleting its cycle vertex gives cycle
length at most 2ν−1. Again P≥h−2ν and S≥h−3ν. With no leaves the same
inequality is vacuous and true. Also d_H=q−h≤ν in both topology branches.

### 2.2 Bad outer intervals and run endpoints

Canonical Section 61 splits the outer walk into q intervals between consecutive
loaded hull vertices. Their lengths ℓ_i satisfy Σ(ℓ_i−1)=x_B. At most x_B
intervals are bad; every other interval is an actual unit hull-side contact.
Thus at least S−x_B same-carrier adjacencies are good. Their nonempty good
runs number at most c+x_B. A run of g edges contributes g−1 internal vertices.
It follows that

\[
 |J|\ge h-4\nu-2x_B,\qquad
 \boxed{\kappa=q-|J|\le5\nu+2x_B.}                      \tag{2}
\]

The bound concerns actual loaded source vertices. In particular, in the low
matching/outer-excess branch ν+x_B=o(D), almost every loaded vertex is in J.

## 3. Every good-fan attachment is exclusive and has an unloaded port

Fix p∈J with carrier a and fan neighbors p_−,p_+. Put
u=(p−a)/D, choose a unit transverse vector v_0, and write

\[
 \epsilon={1\over2D},\quad \tau=\sqrt{1-\epsilon^2},\quad
 p-p_\pm=\epsilon u\pm\tau v_0.
\]

The canonical loaded contact-degree cap is three. If p belongs to any A_r,
it already has the two loaded fan contacts and must have exactly one further
contact pz, with z∈I_r. Hence it belongs to exactly one attachment set and
N_r counts distinct exclusive loaded attachment vertices and their distinct
loaded-to-unloaded contact edges.

For completeness, a third contact is automatically unloaded even before an
attachment set is specified. Let p−z=ru+sv_0. The source diameter bound to
a gives r≥ε; unit separation from p_−,p_+ forces this vector into the inward
30-degree cone, giving

\[
 r\ge{\epsilon+\sqrt3\tau\over2},\qquad
 |s|\le{\tau-\sqrt3\epsilon\over2}<\tfrac12.              \tag{3}
\]

In coordinates with p=0 and a=(−D,0), the fan neighbors are (−ε,±τ).
For D≥9, z=(−r,−s) lies strictly inside their triangle with a: r>ε, r<D,
and |s|<1/2<τ(D−r)/(D−ε). Actual diameter endpoints are extreme source
points, so z has no diameter edge. Its positive contact to p puts it in an I_r.

This uses the actual source triangle and retains inactive constraints; it is
not a harmonic-carrier substitution.

## 4. Linear fan population in every macroscopic actual cell

Let B_r be the number of contacts from I_r to loaded vertices outside J.
Because every good-fan attachment is exclusive,

\[
 t_r=N_r+B_r,\quad
 \sum_rB_r\le3\kappa,
\]

by the loaded degree cap. Combining with (1) gives

\[
 \boxed{N_r=\delta_r+3+s_r+r_r-B_r
 \ge d_r+1+s_r+r_r-B_r.}                               \tag{4}
\]

Consequently, for every cell,

\[
 \boxed{N_r\ge d_r+1+s_r+r_r-15\nu-6x_B.}               \tag{5}
\]

The error can be charged once globally, rather than separately per cell:

\[
 \boxed{\sum_rN_r\ge\sum_rd_r+c_I+s_C+\sum_rr_r-3\kappa.}\tag{6}
\]

These are finite, same-source inequalities. They improve the concentration
mechanism based solely on averaging over c_I components. The cell's actual
attachment incidence, graph diameter and pinned surplus are coupled directly.

In canonical Type II, Section 88 supplies actual harmonic cells with

\[
 d_*\ge(\mu_0-o(1))D,\quad
 \mu_0=0.8896708101\ldots,
 \quad \mu_0/3=6\arcsin\mu_0-2\pi.
\]

Therefore if ν+x_B=o(D), one such cell has

\[
 \boxed{N_*\ge(\mu_0-o(1))D,
 \quad N_*>(0.8896-o(1))D.}                             \tag{7}
\]

No high-t cutoff is needed. This is a linear fan population in one actual
macroscopic harmonic cell, replacing the weaker square-root concentration
from the existing return fork. If a stronger canonical carrier bound applies,
its coefficient substitutes for μ_0 in exactly the same equation.

## 5. Linear deep diameter-inactive ports in that same cell

Each p counted by N_r has a third neighbor z in I_r. A source vertex has at
most five unit neighbors in the triangle-free core, so these N_r incidences
give at least N_r/5 distinct vertices in I_r. They are nonisolated and have
no actual diameter edges.

We also rederive a full-source depth bound. Set h_0=√3/2. An interior source
point at depth <h_0 in the force hull cannot have a unit hull side as its nearest
boundary segment: the perpendicular foot lies in that unit segment, so at
least one endpoint would be at distance <√(1/4+h_0²)=1. A nearest vertex
would directly violate unit separation. Every shallow source point can thus
be assigned to a nonunit hull side, with perpendicular foot in that side.

The bad-side count is at most x_B and their total Euclidean length at most
2x_B, by the canonical outer-walk intervals. For a side of length ℓ, the
assigned points lie in a strip rectangle ℓ by h_0. Their disjoint radius-1/2
disks lie in a rectangle (ℓ+1) by (h_0+1). Summing the resulting area bounds
over the assigned side classes gives

\[
 \#\{z\in A\cap\operatorname{int}F:
        \operatorname{dist}(z,\partial F)<h_0\}
 \le {12(1+h_0)\over\pi}x_B<8x_B.                       \tag{8}
\]

The sum is over assigned disjoint point classes; overlaps between the covering
rectangles do not cause double counting of points. This argument includes
contact isolates in A and supplies no force to them.

Hence I_r contains at least

\[
 \boxed{Z_{r,deep}\ge N_r/5-8x_B}                       \tag{9}
\]

distinct such port vertices at loaded-hull depth ≥h_0. For every one and every
full-source point y, B(z,h_0)⊂F⊂B(y,D), so

\[
 \boxed{|z-y|\le D-h_0.}                               \tag{10}
\]

Using (7), the same macroscopic cell contains

\[
 \boxed{Z_{*,deep}\ge(\mu_0/5-o(1))D
       >(0.17792-o(1))D.}                              \tag{11}
\]

These are actual positive-core vertices protected from every upper-distance
constraint by one fixed margin. This does not make them unit-clear sites.

## 6. Exact noncrossing compression and a joint cell budget

There is a further finite restriction on how ports can be distributed. Choose
any subset E of exclusive loaded attachment vertices, N=|E|, N_r=|E∩A_r|.
Here E need not be the good-fan set; this paragraph reuses N_r for this general
exclusive count. Let g_r count gaps between consecutive members of A_r that
contain vertices of E belonging to other cells.

Canonical Section 83 forbids alternating attachment pairs. Every other cell's
exclusive vertices consequently lie in one A_r-gap; otherwise two such vertices
and two separating A_r vertices would alternate. Thus g_r≤c_I−1.

Delete those N−N_r other-cell vertices from the cyclic loaded order. The retained
cycle has q−N+N_r vertices and contains A_r. Its edges with both endpoints in
A_r number at least 2a_r−(q−N+N_r). At most g_r of those edges were created
by deletion; at most x_B original cyclic adjacencies lack a known unit contact.
Thus the induced loaded contact count c_r=|C[A_r]| obeys

\[
 \boxed{c_r\ge2a_r-q+N-N_r-g_r-x_B.}                   \tag{12}
\]

The canonical local face identity is
L_r+Q_r=4a_r−6−2s_r−2c_r. Also the triangle-free penny-graph diameter bound
for C[I_r∪A_r] gives δ_{K_r}+s_r+c_r≤2a_r−3. Consequently

\[
 \boxed{\delta_{K_r}+s_r+N-N_r
       \le q+g_r+x_B-3,}                               \tag{13}
\]

and

\[
 \boxed{(L_r+Q_r)/2+s_r+N-N_r
       \le q+g_r+x_B-3.}                               \tag{14}
\]

Specialize back to E equal to all good-fan attachment vertices. Apply (4) to
the other cells and charge their B_s once. Since N≤q and Σ B_s≤3κ,

\[
 \boxed{(L_r+Q_r)/2+\sum_{s\ne r}d_s+s_C
       \le q+g_r+x_B-3+3\kappa.}                       \tag{15}
\]

We dropped the nonnegative other-cell r_s and additive constants; the weaker
form (15) avoids any asymptotic assumption. In low matching/outer-excess Type II,
c_I=o(D). Under the explicit additional ledger condition s_C=k+o(D), writing
t_D=(q−k)/D, this becomes

\[
 \boxed{(L_r+Q_r)/2+\sum_{s\ne r}d_s\le t_DD+o(D).}    \tag{16}
\]

Thus the chosen cell's actual outer walk and exceptional-face currency compete
with every other actual cell's diameter in one source budget. Condition
s_C=k+o(D) is stated explicitly; it is not inferred just from ν+x_B=o(D).

## 7. Hostile audit and the continued closing attack

The direct incidence proof in Section 4 is stronger than using (13) and a
global high-t lower bound on N. The latter would give only a safe 0.3111D
cell population at t_D≤1.860. Equation (7) supplies 0.8896D without that
cutoff. The certificate checks both constants but the weaker route is not
presented as the frontier.

Dropping actual noncrossing makes (12) false. In a six-position cyclic packet
take A={0,2,4} and assign the three other positions to one second cell. Its
two alternating triples have crossing convex hulls. The original cycle has
no A–A adjacency, but the false substitution g≤c_I−1=1 would demand two.
This is an exact combinatorial regression, not an actual KKT source or a
counterexample to the canonical noncrossing theorem. Exclusivity is equally
necessary: designating an owner does not delete a vertex shared with A_r.

I next tried to use (7) to force a source triangle from inward spokes. That
fails because each port is inactive only in the diameter graph. Its lower
unit contacts remain active, and its positive harmonic equilibrium may trap
it. Equation (10) supplies upper slack but no vacancy or simultaneous lower
release. The rhombic-collar regression already on PR #627 protects this
distinction. No diameter-inactive vertex is discarded or automatically moved.

The next attack used the actual complete shore in the macroscopic cell. A
linear family of fan boundary directions need not cross both shores; a
direction-preserving train can terminate at an exceptional face or traverse
only one shore. Its stopping endpoint must be charged at boundary order.
The exact budget (16) retains those costs, but it currently permits a single
large cell with ordinary fan ears and a linear internal exceptional-face
population. It does not turn many separate port releases into a compatible
full-source move. No finite competitor is claimed.

The precise remaining obligation is to make a simultaneous lower-feasible
source surgery in the cell singled out by (7)–(11), or prove that its actual
fan-started trains exhaust (16) before supplying the quadratic rhombic core.
The untouched source, every old diameter and all inactive pairs must be retained
until a replacement is certified.

## 8. Computation, dependencies and lifecycle

The verifier exhausts finite Woodall path/odd-cycle leaf packets and good/bad
fan runs, cyclic compression configurations through q=10 with every possible
missing-side count, and integer pinned-incidence identities. It certifies
rational alternating-series bounds for μ_0>0.8896, the 0.17792 coefficient,
and strip arithmetic. Its graph packets omit Euclidean geometry, actual
positive stress, source train placement, Type-II limits and global optimality.
Its cyclic packets encode the gap count directly; the source geometry that
bounds it is proved in Section 6. The analytic proofs above do not follow
from finite enumeration alone.

Dependencies are [C-I restoration](../targets/target-c/56-ci-restored-frontier.md),
[C-ZRF](../targets/target-c/57-zr-zf-rigidity-audit.md), canonical C-WOODALL,
the loaded degree cap in [Target C 03](../targets/target-c/03-pinned-block-and-loaded-boundary-frontier.md),
the outer-walk facts in [Section 61](../targets/target-c/61-linear-nonmatching-excess-audit.md),
the pinned and attachment identities in [Section 62](../targets/target-c/62-attachment-incidence-currency-audit.md),
[Section 75](../targets/target-c/75-all-phase-component-deatomization-audit.md),
the same-source noncrossing proof in [Section 83](../targets/target-c/83-attachment-cell-disjoint-tiling-audit.md),
the Type-II macroscopic carrier in [Section 88](../targets/target-c/88-harmonic-wrapping-diameter-audit.md),
and the exact local face identity in [Section 89](../targets/target-c/89-harmonic-cell-train-budget-audit.md).

No canonical state or active prompt is changed. These claims remain proved
candidates awaiting independent audit/promotion. The macroscopic inactive
container, higher matching, larger x_B, split-star, nonconstant-phase and
other C-II branches are not eliminated. The result is actual macroscopic
cell concentration with globally protected inactive ports, not Level I closure.
